Online Canteen Food-Ordering System

1. Introduction

The Online Canteen Food-Ordering System is designed to make food ordering easier for college students. It allows students to browse food menus, select food items, place orders, make online payments, and receive notifications when their orders are ready.

This system uses Progressive Web Application (PWA) technology to provide a mobile-friendly and user-friendly experience.

2. Mobile and Web Applications

* Mobile Application: Software installed and used on smartphones.
* Web Application: Software accessed through a web browser.
* Progressive Web Application (PWA): A web application that provides mobile-app-like features and can be accessed through a browser.

3. Comparison of Mobile, Web and PWA

Feature	Mobile App	Web App	PWA
Installation	Required	Not required	Optional
Accessibility	Mobile devices	Web browsers	Mobile and desktop
Notifications	Supported	Limited support	Supported
Offline Support	Possible	Limited	Supported
Development Cost	High	Low	Medium

4. Selection of Suitable Application

A Progressive Web Application (PWA) is the most suitable choice for the online canteen food-ordering system.

Reasons:

1. Students can access the application through a web browser.
2. No compulsory installation is required.
3. It supports push notifications.
4. It works on both mobile phones and computers.
5. It is cost-effective and easy to maintain.

5. Four Major Functionalities

1. Menu Browsing

* Students can view available food items.
* Displays food names, prices and descriptions.

2. Order Placement

* Students can select food items.
* Add selected items to the shopping cart.
* Confirm and place orders.

3. Online Payment

* Supports UPI, debit cards and other digital payment methods.
* Provides payment confirmation.

4. Order Notifications

* Students receive updates about their order status.
* Notifications are sent when food is ready for collection.

6. Three Development Challenges

1. Payment Security

Protecting students’ payment information and preventing unauthorized transactions.

2. Real-Time Notifications

Ensuring students receive timely notifications when their food is ready.

3. Performance and Network Issues

Handling multiple students ordering simultaneously and managing slow or unstable internet connections.

